Naturally, this spawned cultural oddities. Chief among them: The Knights of the Blessed Order of the Blown Kleenex, whose annual Cough-It-Up Pageant drew cranky geezers from hundreds of kilometres around. Not content with exchanging anecdotes over cheap bourbon, they began preserving their most revolting expectorants, competing for the coveted Golden Tissue Box. All was well and sickening until Pageant the Fifth, when a veteran entered a specimen that had mutated into an organism so virulent it proved immediately fatal, dissolving the eyes, duodenum, and left kneecap of every host. It even killed brown dogs.\
\
Let that be a lesson: no matter how beneficent a technology looks, never store your snot in a stasis unit.\

